-- title:
--   Original refining BV physical-grid discounted C1 positive Taylor error vanishes in mean from compact source domination
-- statement:
--   For the authentic original bounded-variation spectrally negative Lévy process X and admissible original dividend process D, define the discounted C1 Taylor residual on physical grids exactly via the raw negative-jump sum J, Y=X+J and pre-right-payment reserves. If the grid spans [0,T] with T≤1, its cell segments remain in one compact strictly interior band and the maximum absolute Y increment tends to zero almost surely, while w has common compact Lipschitz and derivative bounds and the exact error is measurable, then the positive parts are integrable and their expectations tend to zero. This theorem derives a.e. convergence from the original physical mesh theorem and uniform domination from the original BV variation and global compact-band Taylor bound, invoking real DCT without importing BV prebudget or signed Fatou conclusions. Cap/ruin contact cells are a separate obligation.
-- source:
--   Proved original BV positive-error DCT 70a2660b-af9a-4e0c-9e31-a0cf5eed04e9; original a.e. physical-mesh adapter avram_bv_error7_original_physical_C1_error_AE_of_refining_grid (publication job cd66105e-a7c4-4e9c-9b32-c59535a54542); original global Taylor BV source domination avram_bv_error7_original_global_C1_Taylor_error_le_BV_source_mass (publication job e451003a-0252-4e20-9db4-e6194b2deded). All dependencies use the real X/D/J/Y, no circular budgets.

